# Allow-list build context: everything is excluded first, then only what the image needs is let back in.
# Excluded on purpose (and never re-included): .git, .github, tests, docs, fixtures, reference, ig, frontend,
# node_modules, data and caches, every .env file, virtual environments, hackathon PDFs and the stack-ia-dev folder.
*

!pyproject.toml
!requirements-lock.txt
!src
!scripts/runtime_requirements.py
!scripts/container_healthcheck.py

# Defence in depth: the allow-list above re-includes src/ as a whole, so a stray dotenv file inside it
# must still stay out (the last matching rule wins).
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Never let compiled or cached files of the developer's machine in (bytecode is compiled inside the image).
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
